{"title":"2023 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nIn the figure below, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/6375cd4bfc64f452328e8a09c67e390aa7225b89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1023$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> total circles. The area between circles alternate between shaded and non-shaded. The area of the shaded region can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da40faccb9c89ca9cfed0f44129b44b014b42639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\pi$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da40faccb9c89ca9cfed0f44129b44b014b42639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\pi$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" />. </p><center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3ee9039bc2687237fe41f7713c9a971561df260b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(5cm); fill(circle((0,0),10),black); fill(circle((0,0),9),white); fill(circle((0,0),8),black); fill(circle((0,0),7),white); fill(circle((0,0),3),black); fill(circle((0,0),2),white); fill(circle((0,0),1),black); dot((0,6)); dot((0,5)); dot((0,4)); [/asy]\" width=\"238\" height=\"238\" /> </center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that  \\begin{align*} k &amp;= 1023^2-1022^2+1021^2-1019^2\\ldots+3^2-2^1+1^2\\\\ &amp;= (1023-1022)(1023+1022)+\\ldots+(3-2)(3+2)+1^2\\\\ &amp;= (1023+1022)+(1021+1019)+\\ldots+(3+2)+1\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1023\\cdot1024}{2}\\implies\\\\ k&amp;\\equiv\\boxed{776}\\pmod{1000}. \\end{align*}\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024417\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.005 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.005 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 25/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 876/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31914:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024417 and revision id 274644. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}